Yes, magic whistles are great.  I usually don't rob shops systematically 
without them (might try however to get one or two desirable items out).

> Any other wisdom?

Well, concerning apport.  If I have a magic whistle, I don't throw more 
than one tripe ration at the pet.  I may be wrong but it seems to me 
that the pet not only picks up things more often with increased apport 
but also drops them more often.  Usually, I stand in the doorway and 
whistle the pet when it has picked up s.th. I want.  I repeat until the 
pet is outside the shop, so I am sure when it drops the item, I can pick 
it up.  This often takes whistling twice, so if the pet drops items too 
frequently, I may have to try more often.

Magic whistles work better with several pets but not too many.  Two 
pets, preferably a dog and a cat (so you know immediately whether you 
have transported the right one out of the shop) are good, four are 
already too many.

I am currently robbing One-eyed Sam with three cats and a dog...

Ah, here's another good trick.  Drop one or several identified valuable 
gems in the shop and sell them.  For diamonds you can get 2000 $ apiece. 
  Then wait until your pet picks them up and whistle it out of the shop. 
  Then buy things with the just earned zorkmids and drop the gems again. 
  This way, you can empty the whole shop (I usually leave the crap in 
there) *and* get all the money of the shopkeeper.  Just sell the same 
gem over and again until you get the message "... offers you only 1700 
zorkmids for your diamond", sell it and have it robbed the final time.
(This does not work well with One-eyed Sam, of course, unless you sell 
20 gems at a time and he has enough cash.)
